inition of $f,$ we have that $f(1,-1)=-1.$ Computing the partial derivatives, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x} & =-{y}^{2}\\, &  & ⇒\\, & {f}_{x}(1,-1)=-1, \\\\ {f}_{y} & =-2xy &  & ⇒\\, & {f}_{y}(1,-1)=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the gradient of the function at the point $(1,-1)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(1,-1) & =⟨-1,2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the linear approximation of the function $f$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & ≈f(1,-1)+∇f(1,-1)\\cdot ⟨x-1,y+1⟩ \\\\  & ≈-1+⟨-1,2⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,y+1⟩ \\\\  & ≈-1-(x-1)+2(y+1) \\\\  & ≈2-x+2y\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186383147 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186383148 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186383147 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186383149 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186383147 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186383150 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186383147 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186383151 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186383147 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186383152 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186383147 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186383147 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186383147 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186383152 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186383147 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "f102ebcb-0a48-5085-94bc-c1ac0bda4076" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186383148 #edb/ref 1080 "f(x,y)≈x-2y" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186383148 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186383148 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "94c81a8f-8b3c-59a9-b3bc-1e3c6f1d0f89" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186383149 #edb/ref 1080 "f(x,y)≈-1+x+y" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186383149 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186383149 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "e7211b05-cdef-52df-b9f5-794f91721ce8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186383150 #edb/ref 1080 "f(x,y)≈-x-y" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186383150 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186383150 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "05323a66-a7b1-5534-8840-c3fe203d1155" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186383151 #edb/ref 1080 "f(x,y)≈-3+x-y" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186383151 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186383151 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "a0e57c79-235f-5c6f-bbb8-7e965feef750" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186383152 #edb/ref 1080 "f(x,y)≈2-x+2y" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186383152 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186383152 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "6a76e60c-a626-557c-88ff-af8b91dc41a9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385906 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186385907 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385906 #edb/ref 1069 "q-98333" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385906 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385906 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $f(x,y)$ be a differentiable function such that\n\n$$\nf(3,2)=9,\\,{f}_{x}(x,y)=-\\frac{3x}{\\sqrt{26-{x}^{2}-2{y}^{2}}},\\,{f}_{y}(x,y)=-\\frac{6y}{\\sqrt{26-{x}^{2}-2{y}^{2}}}.\n$$\n\nUsing a linear approximation of $f$ at the point $(3,2),$ estimate the value of $f(3.05,2.05).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385906 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f3f7ff9e-4535-5200-a21a-2208bf03983f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385906 #edb/ref 1074 "The linear approximation of the function $f$ at the point $(a,b)$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x,y)≈f(a,b)+∇f(a,b)\\cdot ⟨x-a,y-b⟩.\n$$\n\nSo, the linear approximation of $f$ at the point $(3,2)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & ≈f(3,2)+∇f(3,2)\\cdot ⟨x-3,y-2⟩ \\\\  & =f(3,2)+⟨{f}_{x}(3,2),{f}_{y}(3,2)⟩\\cdot ⟨x-3,y-2⟩ \\\\  & =9+⟨{f}_{x}(3,2),{f}_{y}(3,2)⟩\\cdot ⟨x-3,y-2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find ${f}_{x}(3,2)$ and ${f}_{y}(3,2)$ using the given partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(3,2) & =-\\frac{3(3)}{\\sqrt{26-(3)^{2}-2(2)^{2}}}=-3 \\\\ {f}_{y}(3,2) & =-\\frac{6(2)}{\\sqrt{26-(3)^{2}-2(2)^{2}}}=-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nf(x,y)≈9+⟨-3,-4⟩\\cdot ⟨x-3,y-2⟩.\n$$\n\nFinally, we can estimate $f(3.05,2.05)$ by evaluating the linear approximation at $x=3.05$ and $y=2.05,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(3.05,2.05) & ≈9+⟨-3,-4⟩\\cdot ⟨3.05-3,2.05-2⟩ \\\\  & =9+⟨-3,-4⟩\\cdot ⟨0.05,0.05⟩ \\\\  & =9-0.15-0.2 \\\\  & =8.65\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385907 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186385908 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385907 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186385909 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385907 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186385910 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385907 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186385911 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385907 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186385912 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385907 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385907 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385907 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186385909 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385907 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "311374b4-388a-5fad-bc7a-707753d226fa" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385908 #edb/ref 1080 "9.05" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385908 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385908 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "45bb1f2b-4770-5e9f-916d-76839911c3bd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385909 #edb/ref 1080 "8.65" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385909 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385909 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "cbd80317-f861-5477-b55a-d39cc46e39e7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385910 #edb/ref 1080 "8.90" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385910 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385910 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "314ea318-63db-5fd0-ab48-1280dd3d2801" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385911 #edb/ref 1080 "9.10" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385911 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385911 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "d5ae7c85-0f69-5ef6-a022-cca2272fc6b9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385912 #edb/