t the point $(1,0,3)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z) & ≈f(1,0,3)+∇f(1,0,3)\\cdot ⟨x-1,y-0,z-3⟩ \\\\  & =-9+⟨{f}_{x}(1,0,3),{f}_{y}(1,0,3),{f}_{z}(1,0,3)⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,y,z-3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find ${f}_{x}(1,0,3)$, ${f}_{y}(1,0,3)$ and ${f}_{z}(1,0,3),$ using the given partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(1,0,3) & =0 \\\\ {f}_{y}(1,0,3) & =1 \\\\ {f}_{z}(1,0,3) & =-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)≈-9+⟨0,1,-6⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,y,z-3⟩.\n$$\n\nFinally, we can estimate $f(0.98,-0.01,3.1)$ by evaluating the linear approximation at $x=0.98,y=-0.01$ and $z=3.1,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(0.98,-0.01,3.1) & ≈-9+⟨0,1,-6⟩\\cdot ⟨0.98-1,-0.01,3.1-3⟩ \\\\  & =-9+⟨0,1,-6⟩\\cdot ⟨-0.02,-0.01,0.1⟩ \\\\  & =-9-0.01-0.6 \\\\  & =-9.61\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186428468 #edb/ref 1030 0.5 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186428468 #edb/ref 1032 "Initial Codex estimate from captured target-band crossing frequency. Selected account foundations: 1 rises / 2 eligible passed source activities = 0.500000; nearest selected fraction = 1/2. Crossing activity numbers [2]; waits [2]. Separate account estimates: differential=1 (1/1); foundations=1/2 (1/2). Selection: most observations, then lower weight, then account name; no averaging. Single-activity estimates included. Intervening target updates: True. Crossing frequency is the chosen practical estimate of encompassing coverage; a multi-band rise counts once. This does not interpret color steps as physical repetition units. Method: encompassing-report.md. Evidence: reference/mathacademy/encompassing-analysis-2026-10-11/frequency-fractions/foundations-frequency-estimates.json, pair 1937->1934. All account evidence retained in the prepared import's selected-relationships.json." #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186428468 #edb/ref 1036 #edb/ref 17592186050143 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186428469 #edb/ref 1030 1.0 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186428469 #edb/ref 103