 the partial derivatives, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x} & ={y}^{2}\\, &  & ⇒\\,{f}_{x}(-2,-3)=(-3)^{2}=9, \\\\ {f}_{y} & =2xy &  & ⇒\\,{f}_{y}(-2,-3)=2(-2)(-3)=12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the gradient of the function at the point $(-2,-3)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(-2,-3) & =⟨9,12⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the linear approximation of the function $f$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & ≈f(-2,-3)+∇\\,f(-2,-3)\\cdot ⟨x+2,\\,y+3⟩ \\\\  & =-19+⟨9,12⟩\\cdot ⟨x+2,\\,y+3⟩ \\\\  & =-19+9(x+2)+12(y+3) \\\\  & =35+9x+12y.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489315 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186489376 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489315 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "439f497b-63cd-56ed-a071-521a6753dfc6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489315 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186489249 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489322 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186489323 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489322 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "5ad6acc3-0cf4-512b-9839-fcc4716b1315" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489322 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186404946 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489323 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "5e7f4e61-c58d-5ffd-a813-3c6ffee4ea99" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489323 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186265762 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489369 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186489322 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489369 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "d73be3e2-360c-5190-b3b2-da40bf0a43c4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489369 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186489212 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489376 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186489369 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489376 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "e2dfefda-76b1-52f8-a7d5-688673b9ad6c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489376 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186425853 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186504037 #edb/ref 1080 "8.02" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186504037 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186504037 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "046fc72e-76bd-5d